# Real captured pixel data (RGB565LE frame corpora, and the raw RGBA
# mirscreencast originals if not yet cleaned up) is large (single-digit
# GiB) and is not committed to the repository, the same policy already
# applied to backport-4.9/env/local/assets/. The small per-scenario
# metadata sidecars (*.meta.json, *.index.json, *.stderr.log) and the
# derived dedup_stats.json ARE committed -- they are the evidence trail
# (capture parameters, per-frame timestamps, dedup statistics) without the
# bulky pixel payloads.
capture/raw/*.rgba
capture/raw/*.rgb565le

# Broad-benchmark quality-comparison PNGs (original/reconstructed/diff,
# ~207 MiB across the corpus/resolution sweep) are reproducible by
# re-running scripts/run_benchmark.sh and are not committed; every other
# broad-benchmark artifact (results.json/csv, summary.md, environment.json,
# residual-analysis.json, raw/*.json) is committed and preserved.
results/quality/

# Local scratch space for scp/tar staging; never committed.
.scratch/
